CM_ BU_ Mppt "The two MPPTs (maximum power point trackers), named Javed and Woof. Each takes power from part of the solar array and converts it to charge the battery. TODO: add the MPPT make and model, and which part of Peri's solar array each MPPT (Javed, Woof) is connected to.";
CM_ BU_ Telemetry "The telemetry board, which polls the MPPTs (see Telemetry.dbc).";
CM_ BO_ 1905 "Status of the MPPT named Javed, sent in reply to each MpptPollJaved request from the telemetry board (every mppt_update ms, Telemetry/config.txt).";
CM_ SG_ 1905 VoltageIn "Voltage from the solar array into this MPPT (scaling from the MPPT datasheet, as previously applied in live_power.py).";
CM_ SG_ 1905 CurrentIn "Current from the solar array into this MPPT (scaling from the MPPT datasheet, as previously applied in live_power.py).";
CM_ SG_ 1905 VoltageOut "Output voltage of this MPPT (battery side). TODO: add scaling and unit from the MPPT datasheet (still the raw value; check whether it is 208.79 mV per bit, as on similar MPPTs).";
CM_ SG_ 1905 AmbientTemperature "Temperature inside this MPPT. TODO: add scaling and unit from the MPPT datasheet (still the raw value).";
CM_ SG_ 1905 OverTemperature "1 if the MPPT reports that it is too hot.";
CM_ SG_ 1905 NoCharge "1 if the MPPT reports that it is not charging. TODO: add the conditions that set this flag, from the MPPT datasheet.";
CM_ SG_ 1905 UnderVoltage "1 if the MPPT reports an undervoltage. TODO: add whether this is the solar array (input) or battery (output) side, from the MPPT datasheet.";
CM_ SG_ 1905 BatteryVoltageLevelReached "1 if the battery has reached the MPPT's maximum output voltage, so the MPPT is limiting the charge.";
CM_ BO_ 1906 "Status of the MPPT named Woof, sent in reply to each MpptPollWoof request from the telemetry board (every mppt_update ms, Telemetry/config.txt).";
CM_ SG_ 1906 VoltageIn "Voltage from the solar array into this MPPT (scaling from the MPPT datasheet, as previously applied in live_power.py).";
CM_ SG_ 1906 CurrentIn "Current from the solar array into this MPPT (scaling from the MPPT datasheet, as previously applied in live_power.py).";
CM_ SG_ 1906 VoltageOut "Output voltage of this MPPT (battery side). TODO: add scaling and unit from the MPPT datasheet (still the raw value; check whether it is 208.79 mV per bit, as on similar MPPTs).";
CM_ SG_ 1906 AmbientTemperature "Temperature inside this MPPT. TODO: add scaling and unit from the MPPT datasheet (still the raw value).";
CM_ SG_ 1906 OverTemperature "1 if the MPPT reports that it is too hot.";
CM_ SG_ 1906 NoCharge "1 if the MPPT reports that it is not charging. TODO: add the conditions that set this flag, from the MPPT datasheet.";
CM_ SG_ 1906 UnderVoltage "1 if the MPPT reports an undervoltage. TODO: add whether this is the solar array (input) or battery (output) side, from the MPPT datasheet.";
CM_ SG_ 1906 BatteryVoltageLevelReached "1 if the battery has reached the MPPT's maximum output voltage, so the MPPT is limiting the charge.";
CM_ BO_ 1809 "Request from the telemetry board asking the Javed MPPT to send its status (message Javed). Sent every mppt_update ms (Telemetry/config.txt).";
CM_ SG_ 1809 Blank "Not used: the request carries no data.";
CM_ BO_ 1810 "Request from the telemetry board asking the Woof MPPT to send its status (message Woof). Sent every mppt_update ms (Telemetry/config.txt).";
CM_ SG_ 1810 Blank "Not used: the request carries no data.";
